#!/bin/bash
# Dec 036 items 1+3: Codex review of the stock-path gate fix (delta on top of 63127c8). Waits for the 63127c8 probes review
# (which could not be stopped; it still covers P1-P3 + the 31b timing bundle) so Codex runs at most two reviews at once.
set -e
cd /home/ubuntu/work/gemma
for j in review-kernel-probes-light; do
  while [ ! -f ops/jobs/$j.status ] || grep -q '^running' ops/jobs/$j.status; do sleep 60; done
done
export CODEX_EFFORT=medium
exec bin/codex-review 'Review branch codex/kernel-probes-gate (worktree /home/ubuntu/work/gemma-wt/codex-kernel-probes-gate), diff 63127c8..92a74c7 (one commit) in eval/kaggle/timing_summary.py and eval/tests/test_kernel_probes.py. Spec: ops/decisions/036-20261105T212937-908-from-builder.md item 1 and eval/plans/006.md section "Dec 036 correction". The change replaces gate mode minus-image with stock-path: per task setup_py_emulation_seconds = sum of setup_calls duration_s with step == "setup.py" (None if absent/non-numeric), stockpath_phase1_seconds = phase1_wall_seconds - image_emulation_seconds - setup_py_emulation_seconds, gate (b) b_max_stockpath_phase1 = max over tasks <= cap*60+37 (FAIL on any missing value), (c) not gated; probes.h1_composite (not gated) = agent_clock_seconds + finalization_seconds + stock_setup.total_s (None if any part missing or stock_setup.error); default mode total unchanged. KEY CHECK (dec 036 item 3): does (b) in stock-path mode subtract EXACTLY the emulation steps that the stock subprocess path skips (install_editable_package, install_test_dependencies, Dockerfile.public image layers), and NOTHING the scorer would still pay? Map each setup_calls step written by eval/kaggle/agent_timing.py (venv, venv_fidelity, pip_bootstrap, interpreter_probe, tool_sources, pytest_timeout_source, tool_install, tool_deps, pip_check, workspace_editable, base_tar_extraction, setup.py; IMAGE_EMULATION_STEPS at agent_timing.py:833) to what the scorer stock path does: harness source swegemma 0.2.11 at /home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/ (container setup / SubprocessManager path) and eval/tools/stock_subprocess_setup_timing.py (what P1 times). Say which kept steps (venv, workspace_editable, base_tar_extraction) the stock path still pays or not, and whether anything inside the setup.py step (setup_command, SETUP_OBSERVER, base snapshot copy) is something the scorer would still pay outside install_editable_package/install_test_dependencies. Also check: the arithmetic and None handling; that numbers() never rejects a legit value (e.g. a small negative from clock skew); the v5 unit test (fixture copied from results/kaggle_timing_e4b_v001.json on main, rich_3067 -> 89.52 s); that h1_composite is what G1 needs (agent clock + post-cap finalization + stock setup). Mark each finding BLOCKING or NON-BLOCKING. Do not edit files.'
